  "code": "1104",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"110\" data-end=\"306\">The <strong data-start=\"114\" data-end=\"135\">Fructosamine test</strong> measures glycated serum proteins (mainly albumin) to assess average blood glucose levels over the past <strong data-start=\"239\" data-end=\"252\">2&ndash;3 weeks</strong>. It is an alternative to HbA1c, especially useful in:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"308\" data-end=\"572\">\n<li data-start=\"308\" data-end=\"399\">\n<p data-start=\"310\" data-end=\"399\"><strong data-start=\"310\" data-end=\"352\">Monitoring short-term glycemic control</strong> (e.g., during medication changes or pregnancy)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"400\" data-end=\"516\">\n<p data-start=\"402\" data-end=\"516\">Patients with <strong data-start=\"416\" data-end=\"451\">altered red blood cell turnover</strong> (e.g., anemia, hemoglobinopathies) where HbA1c may be unreliable</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"517\" data-end=\"572\">\n<p data-start=\"519\" data-end=\"572\">Assessing glucose control in <strong data-start=\"548\" data-end=\"572\">gestational diabetes</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Fructosamine Level</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>High</strong></td>\n<td>Indicates <strong>poor glycemic control</strong> over recent weeks. May reflect hyperglycemia due to diabetes, stress, steroid use, or acute illness. Often parallels elevated blood glucose or HbA1c trends.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h3 data-section-id=\"srd041\" data-start=\"579\" data-end=\"629\">&nbsp;</h3>",
